            "heading": "Symmetric Block Ciphers: AES & Operational Modes (CBC vs GCM)",
            "text": "The Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) encrypts 128-bit blocks using 128, 192, or 256-bit keys. Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) requires an IV and padding; Galois/Counter Mode (GCM) provides authenticated encryption with associated data (AEAD).",
