            "heading": "Cryptographic Hash Functions & Collision Resistance",
            "text": "Cryptographic hashes (SHA-256, SHA-3) provide fixed-length digests with pre-image, second pre-image, and collision resistance. Legacy algorithms like MD5 and SHA-1 suffer from practical collision attacks and must be deprecated.",
