            "heading": "Keyed-Hash Message Authentication Codes (HMAC)",
            "text": "An HMAC combines a cryptographic hash function with a secret shared key: HMAC(K, m) = H((K' ^ opad) || H((K' ^ ipad) || m)). It provides message integrity and data origin authentication between communicating endpoints possessing the shared key.",
            "codeSnippet": "echo -n 'transaction_data' | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac 'SecretKey123'",
