            "heading": "Rootkits: User-Mode Hooking vs Kernel-Mode Execution",
            "text": "Rootkits conceal unauthorized activities. User-mode rootkits hook APIs in user-space libraries (e.g., injecting DLLs into explorer.exe). Kernel-mode rootkits install malicious drivers (Ring 0) that manipulate kernel object tables (DKOM) to hide processes completely.",
            "codeSnippet": "dmesg | grep -i 'tainted'",
