            "heading": "Web Server Architecture & Virtual Hosting",
            "text": "Web servers (Nginx, Apache) process HTTP requests using event-driven or process-driven architectures. Virtual hosting allows multiple domains on a single IP using the HTTP 'Host' header or TLS Server Name Indication (SNI).",
            "codeSnippet": "cat /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default | grep -E '(server_name|root)'",
            "terminalOutput": "server_name dopilot.org www.dopilot.org;\nroot /var/www/html;",
