            "heading": "HTTP Security Response Headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame)",
            "text": "Modern browsers enforce defensive policies via HTTP response headers: Content-Security-Policy (CSP, restricts script sources), Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS, forces HTTPS), and X-Frame-Options (DENY/SAMEORIGIN, blocks Clickjacking).",
            "codeSnippet": "curl -I https://dopilot.org | grep -E '(Strict-Transport|Content-Security|X-Frame)'",
            "terminalOutput": "Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\nX-Frame-Options: DENY\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'",
