            "heading": "Grover's Algorithm Impact on AES Key Lengths",
            "text": "Grover's quantum algorithm accelerates unstructured database searches, speeding up symmetric brute-force cracking from O(N) to O(sqrt(N)). This effectively halves the security strength of symmetric ciphers: AES-128 is reduced to 64-bit security; AES-256 remains secure at 128-bit.",
            "codeSnippet": "python3 -c 'aes_128_effective = 128 / 2; aes_256_effective = 256 / 2; print(f\"Under Grover: AES-128 -> {aes_128_effective} bits | AES-256 -> {aes_256_effective} bits\")'",
            "terminalOutput": "Under Grover: AES-128 -> 64.0 bits | AES-256 -> 128.0 bits (AES-256 remains quantum-resistant)",
