            "heading": "Hardware Security Module (HSM) Key Isolation & Zeroization",
            "text": "HSMs are physically hardened, tamper-resistant cryptographic appliances certified under FIPS 140-3. Cryptographic private keys are generated and used inside the hardware boundary and physically zeroize (self-erase) if physical tampering is detected.",
