            "text": "TPMs provide hardware security: Platform Configuration Registers (PCRs) store cryptographic measurements of firmware, bootloaders, and OS kernel. 'Data Sealing' encrypts sensitive keys so they can only be decrypted if PCR hashes match exact authorized boot baselines.",
